# Azure deployment plan

## Goal

Provide a clone-and-deploy Azure Developer CLI project for a disposable Odoo ERP/CRM demonstration environment. `azd up` provisions the environment; `azd deploy` intentionally reprovisions the ACI container group to reset the sandbox.

## Project information

- Infrastructure-only `azd` project using Bicep.
- One Azure Container Instances container group.
- Five cooperating containers: PostgreSQL, one-shot Odoo bootstrap, Odoo web, the MCP server, and Caddy HTTPS ingress.
- Images are pulled anonymously from `acrdefcontainer.azurecr.io`; authenticated Azure CLI access is required only to queue builds.
- PostgreSQL and bootstrap state use ACI `emptyDir` volumes, so replacement produces a clean environment.

## Architecture

```mermaid
graph TD
    ACR[acrdefcontainer.azurecr.io] --> ACI[ACI container group]
    Internet -->|80/443| Caddy
    subgraph ACI
        PostgreSQL[(PostgreSQL)]
        Bootstrap[Odoo bootstrap]
        Odoo[Odoo ERP/CRM]
        MCP[MCP server]
        Caddy[Caddy HTTPS ingress]
        BootstrapVolume[(ephemeral readiness volume)]
        DataVolume[(ephemeral PostgreSQL volume)]
        Bootstrap --> PostgreSQL
        Bootstrap --> BootstrapVolume
        PostgreSQL --> DataVolume
        Odoo --> PostgreSQL
        Odoo --> BootstrapVolume
        MCP -->|JSON-RPC| Odoo
        Caddy -->|all other paths| Odoo
        Caddy -->|/mcp| MCP
    end
```

## Security and configuration

- Registry and application passwords are secure Bicep parameters/outputs.
- Application secrets are injected with ACI `secureValue` environment variables.
- Only Caddy ports 80 and 443 are exposed; PostgreSQL, Odoo, and MCP remain internal to the group.
- Caddy automatically manages HTTPS for the generated ACI FQDN and stores certificate state in a group-scoped writable volume.
- Generated demo credentials are printed after provisioning as explicitly requested. They are demo-only and should not be reused.
- The external ACR has anonymous pull enabled, so no registry pull secret is stored in the deployment.

## Execution

1. Create the standard `azure.yaml` and `infra/` project layout.
2. Add modular Bicep for the resource group and ACI container group.
3. Add initialization orchestration and secure outputs.
4. Add cross-platform post-delivery scripts and deployment documentation.
5. Validate Bicep compilation and the `azure.yaml` schema.
6. Do not deploy automatically because the target subscription, location, and private ACR credentials belong to the user.
